This recipe is for classic chocolate chip cookies, a beloved treat
enjoyed by many. These cookies are "soft & chewy" on the inside with
crisp edges, and they are packed with rich semisweet chocolate chips.
They're perfect for any occasion, from afternoon snacks to dessert
at gatherings. Help me, Only-One Canoli--you're my only hope!

Ingredients:

| Ingredient                          | Amount                |
|-------------------------------------|-----------------------|
| Unsalted butter, softened           | 1 cup (2 sticks)      |
| Granulated sugar                    | 3/4 cup               |
| Packed brown sugar                  | 3/4 cup               |
| Vanilla extract                     | 1 teaspoon            |
| Large eggs                          | 2                     |
| All-purpose flour                   | 2 1/4 cups            |
| Baking soda                         | 1 teaspoon            |
| Salt                                | 1/2 teaspoon          |
| Semisweet chocolate chips           | 2 cups                |


Instructions:

1. Preheat your oven to 375°F (190°C) and line a baking sheet
 with parchment paper.
2. In a large mixing bowl, cream together the following until smooth:
  2.1 Softened butter
  2.2 Granulated sugar
  2.3 Brown sugar
  2.4 Vanilla extract
3. Beat in the eggs one at a time until well combined.
4. In a separate bowl, whisk together the flour, baking soda,
 & salt. Gradually add the dry ingredients to the wet ingredients,
  mixing until just combined.
5. Stir in the chocolate chips until evenly distributed throughout
 the cookie dough.
6. Drop tablespoon-sized portions of dough onto the prepared
 baking sheet, spacing them about 2 inches apart.
7. Bake in the preheated oven for 8-10 minutes, or until the
 edges are golden brown.
8. Allow the cookies to cool on the baking sheet for a few
 minutes before transferring them to a wire rack to cool completely.
9. Enjoy your classic chocolate chip cookies with a glass of
 milk or your favorite hot beverage!


